1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,600
[Episode 22]

3
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,150
Oh, please.

4
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:15,950
You're saying

5
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:18,310
the stamp marks on a child

6
00:01:18,310 --> 00:01:20,350
now constitute evidence against me?

7
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:24,310
Oh, please.

8
00:01:24,310 --> 00:01:25,590
Officers,

9
00:01:26,230 --> 00:01:27,310
is this how the police

10
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:29,950
investigate cases now?

11
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:31,790
Mr. Fan,

12
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:32,950
please don't misunderstand.

13
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:34,350
I believe

14
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:36,430
a respected man of your standing

15
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:38,350
would have no dealings with criminals.

16
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:41,710
But on your son's clothes,

17
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:44,280
we found traces of an item
belonging to Sun Jiahao.

18
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,950
So we must follow procedure.

19
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,430
I hope you understand.

20
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:51,950
I understand you,

21
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:54,840
but you need to understand me too.

22
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:57,070
What kind of place is this?

23
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:00,680
How am I supposed to leave?

24
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:02,710
If I do get out,

25
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:05,760
will everyone point fingers at me?

26
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,360
I'll say this one more time.

27
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:12,150
The stamp marks on that child

28
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:14,560
have absolutely nothing to do with me.

29
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,080
Well,

30
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:19,430
perhaps you could

31
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:22,430
look at this another way.

32
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:27,150
Could Jiahao have left those marks

33
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:30,360
accidentally while visiting our home?

34
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:31,150
Director Fan.

35
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,360
You and Sun Jiahao are uncle and nephew,

36
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:36,310
yet you don't seem concerned at all

37
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,030
about his murder.

38
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:40,960
Well,

39
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,840
Jiahao and I were never close.

40
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,960
I never knew when he visited our home.

41
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:52,960
Why did you and Sun Jiahao fall out?

42
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:58,310
That's a family matter.

43
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:00,360
It has nothing to do with your case.

44
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:02,120
Your younger brother,

45
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:03,520
Fan Zhicheng,

46
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,520
married into the Sun family.

47
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,360
He fell ill and died young
from overwork.

48
00:03:08,910 --> 00:03:10,150
How do you feel about that?

49
00:03:11,910 --> 00:03:13,560
I've already told you.

50
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,560
That's a family matter.

51
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,520
It has nothing to do with this case.

52
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,870
You brothers depended on each other

53
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,630
as you made your way out
of the countryside.

54
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,630
His death hit you hard.

55
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:27,750
So you blamed the Sun family,

56
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:29,360
even Sun Jiahao.

57
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:33,240
I can tell you this:

58
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:38,310
I never liked Sun Jiahao.

59
00:03:38,310 --> 00:03:39,310
Satisfied?

60
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,030
He was spoiled from childhood

61
00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:44,910
and became selfish, greedy,
and willful.

62
00:03:44,910 --> 00:03:46,520
I never liked him.

63
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,680
I have nothing to do with him.

64
00:03:57,310 --> 00:03:59,470
If my little brother were still alive...

65
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,080
Sun Jiahao.

66
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:08,840
Sun Jiahao.
Sun Jiahao?
What about him?

67
00:04:09,910 --> 00:04:12,280
Why does that name sound so familiar?

68
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:15,310
Sun Jiahao.

69
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,310
Sun Jiahao.

70
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,830
Why does that name sound so familiar?

71
00:04:18,830 --> 00:04:19,830
Sun Jiahao.

72
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:30,750
Officer,

73
00:04:31,310 --> 00:04:32,040
I...

74
00:04:32,950 --> 00:04:33,950
I lost the note

75
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:36,360
my wife wrote with directions.

76
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,750
Now I can't find my way home.

77
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:38,950
Please.

78
00:04:38,950 --> 00:04:41,750
Could you call my family

79
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:42,750
and ask them

80
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,630
to come get me?

81
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:49,240
We checked with Municipal Hospital
and his family.

82
00:04:49,310 --> 00:04:50,870
He does have Alzheimer's disease,

83
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:52,920
and it's already severe.

84
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,630
Why did he keep it hidden?

85
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,750
He's the director of Rennian Hospital.

86
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,240
If people found out,

87
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:02,480
he'd have to retire early.

88
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,270
How long has he been ill?

89
00:05:05,510 --> 00:05:06,680
It started six months ago.

90
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:09,040
It progressed that quickly?

91
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,000
They said it became severe
two months ago.

92
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,120
He got lost twice.

93
00:05:13,510 --> 00:05:14,630
The local police have records.

94
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:16,510
All within the past two months.

95
00:05:17,310 --> 00:05:18,120
Isn't that too much of a coincidence?

96
00:05:24,270 --> 00:05:25,480
You're not doubting that too, are you?

97
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,360
We have to question every possibility.

98
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:34,630
Who would damage their own brain
to evade questioning?

99
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:35,720
Absurd.

100
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:36,750
Utterly absurd.

101
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:39,510
Captain Ren.

102
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:41,950
We found these at Fan Zhichang's home.

103
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,630
Fan Zhichang said

104
00:05:49,630 --> 00:05:51,070
he always kept work journals.

105
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:54,040
They record more than his work.

106
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:55,920
They also contain childhood memories.

107
00:06:03,870 --> 00:06:06,360
But they're only scattered fragments.

108
00:06:06,750 --> 00:06:07,950
It's like a jigsaw puzzle.

109
00:06:08,830 --> 00:06:11,190
My job is to assemble the whole picture.

110
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:26,160
Don't bully my little brother.

111
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,560
Unable to remember agreed times.

112
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,560
Answers may or may not vary.

113
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:41,480
Persistent daily problems
with thinking and memory.

114
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,310
Answers may or may not vary.

115
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,160
Fifth Uncle.

116
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,160
Captain Ren.

117
00:07:00,310 --> 00:07:02,680
I need you
to verify Fan Zhichang's upbringing

118
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:03,750
and employment history

119
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:06,120
to substantiate my theory.

120
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,720
[Serve the People]

121
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:17,120
Is everyone clear on their task?

122
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:17,920
Yes.

123
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:20,480
Time is short.
Report the situation to Han Ning now.

124
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,070
Yes, Captain.
Move out.

125
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:00,190
You're saying

126
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,310
the seal design on that child

127
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,510
became evidence against me.

128
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:11,040
Is this how the police work now?

129
00:08:19,870 --> 00:08:23,720
You hope to find what you need
in my memories.

130
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,750
You'll probably be disappointed.

131
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:27,750
You're right.

132
00:08:28,830 --> 00:08:30,870
Everyone embellishes their memories.

133
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:34,120
But like a mirror,

134
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,550
they reflect your true self.

135
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,150
All right.

136
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,030
Then tell me.

137
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,630
What is my true self?

138
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,510
Selfish and arrogant.

139
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,120
Lacking empathy.

140
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:52,510
You're even colder than I thought.

141
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:54,750
If I hadn't been that way,

142
00:08:55,630 --> 00:08:57,510
I'd still be stuck in that village.

143
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:00,150
I'd never be who I am today.

144
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:01,630
It appears

145
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,510
your relationship with Sun Jiahao

146
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:05,240
wasn't as bad as you claimed.

147
00:09:05,510 --> 00:09:07,360
He was my brother's son, after all.

148
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,910
My brother and I lost our father young.

149
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:16,510
Village children often bullied us.

150
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,510
He was frail,

151
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,080
so I often protected him.

152
00:09:25,510 --> 00:09:26,510
Cold-blooded?

153
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,750
You're the cold-blooded ones.

154
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:32,720
You say you protected him?

155
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,910
Yes.

156
00:09:36,510 --> 00:09:38,360
After my brother died,

157
00:09:39,630 --> 00:09:41,910
I could never blame Jiahao,
no matter how he misbehaved.

158
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,870
If anyone is to blame,

159
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,150
blame me for growing distant from him.

160
00:09:47,550 --> 00:09:48,910
I failed my little brother.

161
00:09:49,670 --> 00:09:51,670
If that's really true,

162
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,360
why were you the only one
who went to college?

163
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,960
Fan Zhicheng had better grades.

164
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:01,550
The year you entered medical school,

165
00:10:02,270 --> 00:10:03,150
he dropped out.

166
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,200
My guess is

167
00:10:05,550 --> 00:10:06,360
he did it for you.

168
00:10:11,910 --> 00:10:13,910
So who was protecting whom?

169
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:15,510
You little fool.

170
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:18,510
You silly little fool.

171
00:10:18,550 --> 00:10:25,910
Little idiot, little fool.
Idiot, idiot, fool, fool.

172
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,720
Fan Zhicheng was more mature than you

173
00:10:29,030 --> 00:10:29,910
and kinder too.

174
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,510
Big brother, take a big bite.

175
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:37,720
Although you were the older brother,

176
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,480
he was usually the one caring for you.

177
00:10:45,670 --> 00:10:46,910
After Fan Zhicheng died,

178
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:50,030
you carried guilt toward him

179
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:53,270
and set up Luoda
for his only child.

180
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:54,750
Right?

181
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:57,240
That's my first hypothesis.

182
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:02,960
You inadvertently helped Sun Jiahao
build a criminal empire.

183
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:06,550
By the time you discovered it,
it was too late to stop him.

184
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,720
So you chose to look the other way.

185
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:10,480
Am I right?

186
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,240
Han Ning!

187
00:11:42,630 --> 00:11:44,150
[Fan Zhichang: Professional Record]
We checked Fan Zhichang's network.

188
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,270
We found no problems.

189
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,120
Hear that?

190
00:11:52,630 --> 00:11:55,550
If I had set up Luoda for him,

191
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:58,000
there would have been some trace of it.

192
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,910
Your theory is wrong.

193
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:45,080
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

194
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:47,030
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

195
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:48,940
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

196
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:50,740
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

197
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:53,080
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

198
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:55,510
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

199
00:12:58,650 --> 00:13:00,560
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

200
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,450
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

201
00:13:02,450 --> 00:13:04,400
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

202
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,520
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

203
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:08,530
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

204
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:10,690
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

205
00:13:14,290 --> 00:13:17,770
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

206
00:13:17,770 --> 00:13:21,140
♪Why is that child crying?♪

207
00:13:21,370 --> 00:13:23,840
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

208
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,460
♪Means I've grown up♪

209
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:28,610
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

210
00:13:28,610 --> 00:13:32,090
♪The wound still aches♪

211
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:36,850
♪Like a biting winter♪

212
00:13:36,850 --> 00:13:40,120
♪But a spark still glows♪

